# Plain JavaScript: no written type asks the key for a number. The turn that finds a cell taken goes round; the others read four lists in a method that is copied in line: two of the file, under the
# counter, and two in fields, under what the first two give. None of the four was asked in front: the reads of the variables and of the slots stayed in the turn, because not every turn comes by them; a test
# could be laid in front only from a block that every turn passes; and the key kept its hole, so the read under it left the typed copy without a test: every turn that did any work ran as written.
# A slot that constructions fill and a variable that is filled at every read fail nowhere, and a proven list can fail in front by the kind of its storage alone: they are asked in front, as the look does
# for lists in the loop's own text. A hole among the keys leaves the turn.
# f3 = weigh
# RUN: walk f3 mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# CHECK-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CHECK-COUNT-2: i32 @Int32 = GetArrayElement {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32 level=Proven [keyIsIntegral, isPresent]
# CHECK: undefined|i32 @OptionalInt64 = GetArrayElement {{*}}arrayStorage=Int32 level=Proven [keyIsIntegral]
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = answers => print(answers.join(" "));
